  "notes": "{披露|ひろう} means to formally present, reveal, or display something to others, often for the first time. It carries a sense of ceremony and public showing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {披露|ひろう}{宴|えん}: reception, announcement party\n- {結婚|けっこん}{披露|ひろう}{宴|えん}: wedding reception\n- {腕前|うでまえ}を{披露|ひろう}する: to display one's skill\n- {新曲|しんきょく}を{披露|ひろう}する: to perform a new song\n- {研究|けんきゅう}{成果|せいか}を{披露|ひろう}する: to unveil research results\n\nRELATED FORM:\nお{披露|ひろ}め is a polite variant meaning 'debut' or 'first public showing.' Often used for new products, buildings, or when introducing someone: お{披露|ひろ}め{会|かい} (unveiling event, debut party).\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal. In casual speech, {見|み}せる (to show) or {発表|はっぴょう}する (to announce) are more common alternatives.",
